WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.667
The dot product combines matching values and weights into a single result.

00:00:04.667 --> 00:00:11.767
Suppose we have several features, such as attendance, assignment performance, and exam performance,

00:00:11.767 --> 00:00:14.297
and each feature has a different weight.

00:00:14.297 --> 00:00:20.182
Multiplying the values by their weights and adding the results produces a weighted score.

00:00:20.641 --> 00:00:27.583
This same mathematical pattern appears in linear regression, classification models, neural networks,

00:00:27.583 --> 00:00:32.128
recommendation systems, and many other machine learning methods.

00:00:32.128 --> 00:00:35.503
NumPy can calculate the dot product directly.

00:00:35.503 --> 00:00:41.663
This slide is useful because it connects basic array operations to the mathematics you will encounter later in machine

00:00:41.663 --> 00:00:43.404
learning.
